Syntax: homestead [return|status|survey|help]

Homesteads are the foundation for future player-built homes, crafted rooms,
and shared kingdom spaces. The kingdom commons is meant to be explored in
character: speak aloud near the surveyor, clerk, and foreman, and they will
answer what they understand.

Current commands:

  homestead          Travel to the kingdom commons.
  homestead return   Return to the room remembered when you entered.
  homestead status   Show your current homestead state.
  homestead survey   Review what is currently available.
  homestead resources
                     Show the rough resource nodes on your plot.
  homestead storage  Show construction materials saved with your plot.
  homestead tools    Show primitive tools saved with your plot.
  homestead gather <material>
                     Gather branch, stone, clay, or grass while standing
                     on your plot.
  homestead make <tool>
                     Make a stone axe, stone mallet, digging stick, or
                     woven basket on your plot.
  homestead visit <player>
                     Visit another player's public or invited plot.
  homestead public   Let anyone visit your plot.
  homestead private  Restrict visits to yourself and invited players.
  homestead invite <player>
                     Invite a player to visit your private plot.
  homestead uninvite <player>
                     Remove a plot invitation.

Useful things to try in the commons:

  say I want land
  say how much does a plot cost
  say I accept the charter
  say take me to my plot
  say what should I build first
  read charter
  study map
  read ledger

A frontier charter costs 1,000,000 coins and grants one tiny staked plot.
The clerk draws from clear bank funds first, then coin on hand. Professions
will help with later work, but they are not required to begin.

Brant explains starter work, but construction happens on your own plot:

  build camp marker    25,000 coins, about 1 minute
  build lean-to        75,000 coins, about 5 minutes
  build foundation    250,000 coins, about 15 minutes

Build timers are saved by the homestead daemon. They continue across logout,
reboot, or crash because the completion time is stored with your plot. More
material-heavy construction will arrive as the system grows.

Once you are standing on your plot, use 'commons' or 'return to commons' to
walk the survey road back.

Rough plot materials:

  gather branch
  gather stone
  gather clay
  gather grass

These materials are saved with your plot instead of carried in inventory.
Each resource node is briefly depleted after gathering, then recovers. Use
'homestead resources' to see which nodes are ready and 'homestead storage'
to see the construction materials available for future work.

Primitive plot tools:

  make stone axe
  make stone mallet
  make digging stick
  make woven basket

Primitive tools are also saved with your plot. They are the first layer of
the construction chain and will feed later workstation and recipe work.

Shaping your plot:

  homestead title <room title>
  homestead describe <room description>
  homestead look add <noun> = <description>
  homestead look remove <noun>

These commands work while you are standing on your own plot. Text is bounded
and saved by the homestead daemon. This first version is descriptive only:
it lets you shape what visitors read and inspect, but it does not run custom
scripts or create arbitrary commands.
